      "id": "i13wea1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Constitutional Amendment"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 368 under Part XX governs the constitutional amendment process in India.",
        "Amendments are categorized into Simple Majority, Special Majority, and Special Majority with State Ratification.",
        "Federal provisions require approval from at least half of the state legislatures before enactment.",
        "Parliament's power to amend the Constitution is limited by the judicial Basic Structure Doctrine."
      ],
      "id": "096qyz7"
    },
