    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 368 specifies the power and procedure of Parliament to amend the Constitution.",
        "State ratification for federal amendments requires a simple majority in state legislatures.",
        "The Basic Structure Doctrine restricts Parliament from altering the core framework of the Constitution."
      ],
